---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { getApp, COMPANY } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('tabloom')!;
const updatedDate = 'August 22, 2026';
const sections = [
  { href: '#availability', label: 'Availability and identity' },
  { href: '#offline', label: 'Offline reading' },
  { href: '#export', label: 'Export, Trash, and history' },
  { href: '#ai', label: 'AI, OCR, and quotas' },
  { href: '#deletion', label: 'Account deletion gap' },
  { href: '#troubleshooting', label: 'Troubleshooting' },
  { href: '#contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  app={app}
  title={`${app.name} Support — ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description="Help with Tabloom private web access, Microsoft identity, guest sharing, explicit offline reading, exports, Trash, history, AI/OCR quotas, and the current account-deletion gap."
  path="/tabloom/support"
  page="support"
  heading="Tabloom Support"
  documentMeta={`Updated ${updatedDate} · Private web app and installable PWA`}
  summary="Tabloom is a private Microsoft-authenticated notebook workspace for one owner and invited guests. It can be installed as a PWA, but offline access is explicit, bounded, and read only. There is no native mobile app or public account registration."
  sections={sections}
  evidenceNote="Support guidance was reviewed against the current Tabloom default branch and its matching live deployment on August 22, 2026."
>
  <section id="availability" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Availability, Microsoft identity, and sharing</h2>
    <p class="legal-callout">
      Tabloom has no public self-service sign-up. Microsoft identity authorizes the
      owner and invited guests. A share is tied to the invited email and role; it
      does not merge Microsoft accounts or create a public notebook.
    </p>
    <p>
      If access is missing, confirm the intended Microsoft account and ask the
      notebook owner to verify the invitation email and role. Support will not ask
      for a password, verification code, Microsoft token, or browser identity key.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="offline" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Explicit offline reading</h2>
    <p>
      Download a notebook while connected to create a sanitized read-only copy in
      identity-scoped IndexedDB. A bounded recent-page setting can also retain
      eligible pages. Offline copies are not end-to-end encrypted and can be read
      by someone with access to that browser profile.
    </p>
    <p>
      Offline mode does not support editing, creation, deletion, sharing, scans,
      AI, Search, Inbox, Trash, live History, or server settings. Reconnecting does
      not immediately enable editing: Tabloom first completes an authoritative
      refresh. If it cannot, the copy stays read only.
    </p>
    <p>
      Sign-out clears private offline stores and is blocked if that clear fails.
      Before sharing or disposing of a device, remove downloaded notebooks or
      clear Tabloom site data in the browser.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="export" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Exports, Archive, Trash, and History</h2>
    <p>
      Tabloom provides page, notebook, and workspace exports. The default workspace
      export is a ZIP containing Markdown pages, notebook indexes, optional link
      listings, and referenced or Media-tab attachments by default. HTML is also
      available; the PDF option creates printable HTML for browser print-to-PDF.
      Exports do not include the Microsoft account or independent provider records.
    </p>
    <p>
      Archive is reversible and does not free stored content. Trash is retained for
      up to 30 days before the daily permanent-delete sweep. Page History keeps the
      latest 50 versions per page. Restore content before those limits if you need
      it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Operator backups are different from exports: verified local SQLite-and-upload
      bundles are retained for 14 days. They are used for service recovery and are
      not available as a self-service account download.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="ai" class="legal-section">
    <h2>AI, semantic search, OCR, and quotas</h2>
    <p>
      Anthropic handles selected generation requests, Voyage AI creates semantic
      embeddings, Azure Computer Vision Read API performs configured OCR, and a
      configured Azure OpenAI gpt-image-1 deployment can clean a selected Inkbox
      scan into a PDF. If a provider is disabled or unavailable, Tabloom reports a
      failure instead of treating the operation as successful.
    </p>
    <p>
      The current per-identity limits are 30 admitted requests in a rolling hour
      and a $5 estimated monthly processing budget. Wait for the rolling window or
      next monthly period after a quota message; repeatedly retrying does not move
      the request to another identity. Generated and extracted output should be
      checked against the original.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="deletion" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Current account-deletion gap</h2>
    <p>
      Tabloom does not currently have a self-service account-deletion control or
      account-deletion API. Emptying Trash or permanently deleting a notebook is
      content deletion, not Microsoft-account or full Tabloom-account deletion.
    </p>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>
      to request a manual review of Tabloom-held account data. The request does not
      delete the underlying Microsoft account, another identity’s records, or
      provider-held operational data, and it is not an immediate automated action.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="troubleshooting" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Troubleshooting checklist</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Confirm the intended Microsoft identity and notebook role.</li>
      <li>Reconnect and wait for a complete authoritative refresh before editing.</li>
      <li>
        For offline issues, remove and redownload the affected notebook while
        connected.
      </li>
      <li>Check Trash and History before assuming recent content is permanently gone.</li>
      <li>
        Record the browser, operating system, time, notebook or page title, and
        visible recovery message for support.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Do not send Microsoft credentials, private tokens, full notebook exports, or
      unredacted personal scans unless support requests a specific safe sample.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Contact and legal documents</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> for product
      help. Read the <a href="/tabloom/privacy">Tabloom Privacy Policy</a> for
      identity, processor, storage, quota, retention, and deletion details. Use of
      Tabloom is subject to the <a href="/terms">Nintek Terms of Use</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
